From a0ba68f6d3e78e04ea5daeacc5562051885126d6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 15:13:20 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] Write the sequence globals once per sequence and copy them
 into each run file

make_run_files wrote every sequence global's expression, units and expansion
as separate HDF5 attributes in every run file. They are now written once per
sequence to an in-memory HDF5 file, and its groups are copied into each run
file. make_single_run_file uses the same path.

For the 100-shot scan of a lab's drop_mot experiment (174 sequence global
attributes), making a run file takes 24 ms instead of 45 ms on the lab's
computer while BLACS and lyse run, and 8 ms instead of 16 ms on a laptop. The
globals groups, attributes and attribute types of all 100 run files are the
same as before.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_012E5FGDFW9HEH6h6shrHpsD
